<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian farm lobby says Hanson threatens trade.</title>
<headline>Australian farm lobby says Hanson threatens trade.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's farm lobby on Thursday joined a chorus of criticism of far-right politician Pauline Hanson and said her views threatened rural trade with Asia.</p>
<p>National Farmers' Federation president Donald McGaughie told a seminar in Melbourne that food exports to the region were vulnerable to Hanson's stance against Asian immigration.</p>
<p>Australia's food exports to Asia are estimated to earn A$16 billion in foreign income by year 2000, he said.</p>
</text>
